{"id": "EUVD-2026-97879", "enisaUuid": "cbf240b4-60e6-3221-a02e-c46d2c72185f", "description": "EdgeEver Desktop 1.92.0 through 1.112.0 contains a remote code execution vulnerability in the desktop:acp-probe IPC handler, which lacks a sender check and spawns a caller-supplied input.path executable. Attackers with script execution in a renderer, such as via template-preview or drag-preview stored cross-site scripting, can call probeAcpAdapter to launch local executables with the user's privileges.", "datePublished": "2026-10-12T20:55:12", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-12T20:55:12", "baseScore": 7.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:L/UI:A/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/tianma-if/edgeever/issues/532", "https://github.com/tianma-if/edgeever/issues/546", "https://github.com/tianma-if/edgeever/commit/6b5027e8b4becbee0c0de7cd1a3d04af78ca87ca", "https://github.com/tianma-if/edgeever/blob/f6ade70423ba366077653dbb8ac43a677933c776/apps/desktop/src/main/acp-host.mjs#L1145", "https://github.com/tianma-if/edgeever", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/edgeever-desktop-1.92.0-through-1.112.0-local-program-execution-via-acp-ipc"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-109556", "GHSA-x8jx-mq2j-m3pv"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.51, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "51d4fe12-f0fc-347d-aace-801c71fc7596", "product": {"name": "EdgeEver", "vendor": {"name": "tianma-if"}}, "product_version": "1.92.0 \u22641.112.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "b9367d0e-2bf1-324f-b3b5-ba34479c483f", "vendor": {"name": "tianma-if"}}], "isExploited": false}